# =============================================================================
# PROJECT audit rules (tools/audit.rules) — RenderEngine
# It is DATA, not framework logic. The engine (tools/audit.sh) runs these plus
# built-in generic checks (branch on main, no warning-suppression flags/pragmas,
# state-file schema, no tracked binaries outside allowed dirs).
#
# Format: name<TAB>mode<TAB>target<TAB>message
# Modes:
#   forbid_grep    regex            fail if regex found in source dirs
#   require_grep   regex            fail if regex NOT found in source dirs
#   forbid_flag    token            fail if token appears in build files
#   forbid_pragma  token            fail if token appears in source files
#   forbid_ext     ext,csv          fail if tracked files carry these extensions
#   forbid_outside dir|regex        fail if regex matches any source OUTSIDE dir
#                                  (the FIRST '|' splits dir from regex, so the
#                                  regex may itself contain '|' alternations)
#   require_only   dir|regex        fail if regex matches outside dir AND has a match inside dir
#   comment_context regex           fail if any comment block matching regex has
#                                  <120 chars of explanatory prose in the block
#                                  (citations excluded from the count); waivers
#                                  via tools/comment_context.allow ERE lines
# '#' lines are comments. Source-scanning rules scan ONLY the directories in
# AUDIT_SOURCE_DIRS (default: io data volume scene core broker render app utils test_utils tests via tools/env.sh).
# If your owning-module rule must cover dirs outside the defaults, override
# AUDIT_SOURCE_DIRS in env (or add those dirs) or the audit can't see them.
# Rules are skipped when no source dirs exist yet; build-file rules are skipped
# when no build files exist yet.
#
# NOTE: project layout uses io/ data/ volume/ scene/ core/ broker/ render/ app/ utils/ test_utils/ tests/, so
# AUDIT_SOURCE_DIRS must be exported via tools/env.sh (see audit.sh env or
# run_task.sh) for the ownership/forbidden rules below to take effect.
# =============================================================================

# --- Hard-coded secrets anywhere in the tree (generic, keep this one) ----------
no_secrets	forbid_grep	(api[_-]?key|password|secret)\s*=\s*["'][A-Za-z0-9+/]{12,}	hard-coded secrets are forbidden

# --- Dependency lock: every FetchContent_Declare must carry a pinned GIT_TAG ---
# (must be a release tag or commit SHA, never a branch name; the mechanical
# floor below rejects common branch names in every build file incl. the root
# CMakeLists.txt, reviewer verifies the rest; pinned tags: glfw 3.4, glad2 v2.0.8 (73db193), glm 1.0.1, imgui v1.92.9, googletest v1.15.2, spdlog v1.14.1, stb 2c980bb59875b0d32144a71867fbdebb2f77cd20, json v3.11.3 — see docs/spec/techstack.md §2 and docs/spec/assets.md)
deps_pinned	require_grep	FetchContent_Declare\([^)]*GIT_TAG	dependencies must be pinned via FetchContent GIT_TAG
deps_pinned_no_branch	forbid_flag	GIT_TAG\s+["']?(master|main|HEAD|develop|feature|release|hotfix|branch)\b	dependencies must pin a release tag or commit SHA, never a branch name

# --- GL ownership & RHI: raw GL calls ONLY under core/rhi/gl/ via IRHIContext (SPEC §3/§6 EOL) -------
# render/, app/, tests/, broker/, scene/, and utils/ must go through core/rhi/ wrappers (IRHIContext); io/, data/, volume/ are GL-free.
# V3 tightens the anchor: raw gl* must be confined to core/rhi/gl/ (one RHI impl); core/ outside that (e.g., core/window.cpp, core/load_core_gl.cpp keep their probes) is allow-listed as anchor until V3.2a RHI lands.
# Transitional (until (stretch) RHI lands (`core/rhi/gl/` appears) audit tightens to core/rhi/gl/): gpu_api_ownership keeps `core|` anchor; rhi_ownership is the V3 hard anchor (activate when `core/rhi/gl/` appears — keep commented until then, see stretch RHI + docs/spec/guardrails.md §6) — see docs/spec/guardrails.md §6 transitional note.
# test_utils/ PixelReader façade must call REContext::readRgba8, not raw gl* — raw stays core-only, façade is via REContext.
gpu_api_ownership	forbid_outside	core|\bgl[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*\(	raw GL calls only under core/ (transitional; tightens to core/rhi/gl/ after V3.2a RHI lands; test_utils façade via REContext, not raw)
# rhi_ownership	forbid_outside	core/rhi/gl|\bgl[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9]*\(	raw GL calls only under core/rhi/gl/ via IRHIContext (activate when core/rhi/gl/ exists; SOLID DIP + OCP for Vulkan)
# New audit anchor: no raw gl* outside core/ at all (already covered) AND no core/rhi/gl/*.hpp include outside broker/render/core (DIP — scene/io/data/volume may never include RHI)

# --- Legacy fixed-function API must never appear anywhere ----------------------
# glBegin is word-boundary anchored so the legacy immediate-mode entry point
# (glBegin(...)) stays banned while core GL 3.0+ transform feedback
# (glBeginTransformFeedback, used by SliceRenderer's cross-section capture,
# T11) is NOT a legacy call and must not be flagged.
no_legacy_api	forbid_grep	\bglBegin\b|glMatrixMode|glOrtho|glFrustum	legacy fixed-function API is forbidden

# --- Readback discipline: raw readback calls only under core/ ------------------
# (single-GL-owner rule; readback is consumed by tests for verification)
# Raw glReadPixels/glGet* stays exclusive to core/re_context.cpp (sole anchor);
# test_utils/ façade (test_utils::PixelReader) must go via REContext::readRgba8, not raw — audit stays core-only.
no_production_readback	forbid_outside	core|\b(glMapBufferRange|glGetBufferSubData|glReadPixels|glGetTexImage|glGetTexLevelParameteriv)\b	readback raw calls only under core/ (test-consumed; test_utils façade via REContext, not raw)

# --- Logging discipline: no raw printf/cout for diagnostics --------------------
no_raw_diagnostics	forbid_grep	std::cout|std::cerr|\bprintf\(	logging discipline: use spdlog, not printf/cout

# --- Asset licensing: every dataset dir must carry a LICENSE file --------------
# Per-dataset-dir LICENSE is enforced mechanically by BOTH the T2 gate (`test -f data/meshes/LICENSE && test -f data/volumes/LICENSE`) AND the built-in audit.sh per-dir checks (`audit.sh: assets licensed per-dir (meshes/volumes)`); grep is floor only for content.
# Audit floor (one LICENSE anywhere) catches zero-license repo; per-dir completeness is `audit.sh` built-in + T2 per-dir gate (mechanical, not review-only).
assets_licensed	require_grep	LICENSE	at least one LICENSE present (floor only); per-dataset-dir LICENSE enforced by audit.sh built-in `assets licensed per-dir` + T2 gate `test -f data/meshes/LICENSE && test -f data/volumes/LICENSE` (SPEC §7)

# --- Disposition / layer isolation (SPEC §3/§6) ----------------------------------
# scene/ is RE-free + GL-free; render/ never includes scene/; broker/ is the
# only library that may include both scene/ and render/.
# scene/ may include data/ + volume/ + glm only — never render/ or core/ GL.
# NOTE: enforced after V3.1 lands (scene/ + broker/ created); until then the
# concrete forbid is review-only to avoid false positives on docs/examples.
# Disposition / layer isolation — mechanical forbid_inside (SPEC §3/§6, broker is only lib that may include both)
disposition_scene	forbid_inside	scene|#include.*render/	re::scene must never include render/ (broker owns the mediation)
disposition_render	forbid_inside	render|#include.*scene/	re::render must never include scene/ (broker owns the mediation)

# --- Bridge completeness + rendering hygiene (SPEC §6) --------------------------------
render_no_glad	forbid_inside	render|#include.*glad	<glad/gl.h> must not appear outside core/ (GL constants via core wrappers; audit render_no_glad_include)
# engine_depth_default	require_grep	setDepthConfig\(	true	Engine facade must default DepthConfig true for mesh views (T8b/T17 divergence, View owns DepthConfig value object)  # activate at T8b (future)
render_no_window	forbid_inside	render|#include.*window\.hpp  # T4 window-free — active now (render/offscreen must not include window.hpp)	render/offscreen must not include window.hpp (T4 window-free, render is GL-constant-only)
# layer_count	require_grep	Count\s*=\s*8  # activate at T8 (8 layers) when scene/layer.hpp exists	Layer Count must stay 8 (T8, 8 layers Background…OverlayTop)
# layer_mask	require_grep	using LayerMask = uint32_t  # activate at T8 when scene/layer.hpp exists	LayerMask must stay uint32_t 1u<< (T8, future-proof)
no_noop_broker	forbid_inside	broker|Noop	broker/ must not contain Noop/placeholder renderables (bridge completeness; every scene kind routes to real layer or typed error)

# --- Broker mediation: one file per mapper + ISP segregation (SPEC §11 SOLID) ----------
# The broker/ mediation is heavily abstracted — one IMapper<AppT,ReT> (pure) or ICachedMapper<AppT,ReT> per file
# (camera_mapper, plane_mapper, *material_mapper, *object_mapper, view_bridge, view_synchronizer, view_compositor).
# IMapper vs ICachedMapper is ISP segregation: a pure mapper must not expose mapCached/invalidate (fat interface).
# A single header that defines translate/mapper for more than one AppT is forbidden. ViewBridge is a SRP-split coordinator
# (ViewSynchronizer + ViewCompositor), not a God mapper.
# This floor rule greps for two distinct "Mapper" class names in one file; the review gate enforces the full one-file-per-type policy.
broker_per_type	forbid_grep	class.*Mapper.*\n.*class.*Mapper	broker/ must be one IMapper/ICachedMapper per file (heavily abstracted per-type mappers, ISP-segregated; ViewBridge is coordinator)
isp_mapper_forbid	forbid_grep	class\s+\w+Mapper\s*:\s*public\s+IMapper[^{]*\{[^}]*mapCached	IMapper must not expose mapCached (ISP — use ICachedMapper)
# srp_viewbridge	forbid_grep	class\s+ViewBridge[^{]*\{[^}]*(sync|renderAll|presentAll)[^}]*sync[^}]*renderAll[^}]*presentAll.*\{	(optional RHI review check — ViewBridge should delegate to ViewSynchronizer/ViewCompositor, not own both caches)

# --- Persistence: never id-only or size-dump sync (SPEC §10) -----------------
# See SPEC §10.1 — CompositeKey{LayoutId,Id,Gen,Hash}, not bare id/size.
# Mechanical floor (recreateAll/dumpAll) is review-only until V3.5 lands.
no_dump_sync	forbid_grep	recreateAll|dumpAll	never use id-only or size-dump recreate-all sync (use generation/contentHash cache)

# --- RE-minimal / asset indirection (SPEC §7/§12) ---------------------------
# render/re_scene must not store verbatim copies of data::Mesh voxels/positions or
# data::VolumeDataset voxels — only derived handles (AssetHandle, Texture3D*, ReMaterial*).
# Active since T9 V3.8 — render/re_scene/ landed.
asset_indirection	forbid_grep	data::Mesh::positions|data::VolumeDataset::voxels	render/re_scene must not store verbatim app asset data (RE-minimal, use handles)

# --- Broker app-reach rule (SPEC §11) ---------------------------------------
# app/ must not hold a broker mapper handle directly (must go through ViewBridge).
broker_app_reach	forbid_grep	broker.*IMapper|broker.*Mapper.*translate	app must not hold a broker mapper handle directly (use ViewBridge façade)

# --- Tests must not include Window directly (SPEC §8, T15 — active from T15, review-only until T15 lands) ---
# Tests use only offscreen context via utils::OffscreenContext delegating to core.
# Enforced from T15 GlfwRuntime onwards; until T15 lands violations are review-gated (transitional) — after T15 the gate `grep -R "window\\.hpp" tests/ ==0` must pass:
test_window_forbid	forbid_inside	tests|#include.*core/window\.hpp	tests must not include core/window.hpp — use offscreen context (T15 GlfwRuntime)

# --- ACL: app never includes render/ (SPEC §3/§11, broker/README) -----------
# The scene→render mediation is broker's monopoly: app expresses scenes as
# scene/ values and drives the IViewBridge façade; render/ types enter app
# source files only through broker headers. Enforced since T20 (all samples
# routed through AppContext + IViewBridge; previously review-only).
acl_app_render	forbid_inside	app|#include[[:space:]]*["<]render/	app must never include render/ directly (route through the IViewBridge façade; broker owns the scene-to-render mediation)

# --- Ownership discipline (T13, user mandate 2026-08-23) ----------------------
# No raw pointers where ownership/lifetime matters. scene/, broker/ and app/
# must not DECLARE a raw pointer (members, parameters, returns, locals) unless
# the borrow is explicitly marked by writing the marker comment between the
# star and the identifier:
#
#     Type* /*borrow*/ name
#
# A marked borrow MUST also carry a Doxygen `@note lifetime:` tag naming its
# owner (review-gate enforced; see docs/spec/guardrails.md "Ownership
# discipline"). The marker breaks the mechanical pattern below, so the
# allowlist of documented borrows is exactly the set of `/*borrow*/` sites,
# each individually reviewable via `rg '/\*borrow\*/'`. Everything else uses
# unique_ptr (sole owner), shared_ptr (shared owner), weak_ptr (observer), or
# a generational handle (AssetHandle / AssetId). The rule scans .hpp AND .cpp:
# sample classes define members in app/*.cpp, and scope-bounded borrows there
# are just as visible and just as markable.
#
# Pattern: `(const )?[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*\*[[:space:]]*[a-z_]` — an identifier
# starting with an uppercase letter, star attached to it, then a lowercase
# name (this project's `Type* name` pointer style). Map-key/template-argument
# stars (`Map<Key*, Value>`) do NOT match (followed by ',' or '>'), and
# multiplication (`A * b`) does not match (space before the star).
ownership_raw_ptr_scene	forbid_inside	scene|(const[[:space:]]+)?[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*\*[[:space:]]*[a-z_]	scene/ must not declare unmarked raw pointers — mark documented borrows `Type* /*borrow*/ name` + @note lifetime: owner, or use smart/handle types
ownership_raw_ptr_broker	forbid_inside	broker|(const[[:space:]]+)?[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*\*[[:space:]]*[a-z_]	broker/ must not declare unmarked raw pointers — mark documented borrows `Type* /*borrow*/ name` + @note lifetime: owner, or use smart/handle types
ownership_raw_ptr_app	forbid_inside	app|(const[[:space:]]+)?[A-Z][A-Za-z0-9_]*\*[[:space:]]*[a-z_]	app/ must not declare unmarked raw pointers — mark documented borrows `Type* /*borrow*/ name` + @note lifetime: owner, or use smart/handle types

# --- Evidence rule + regression lock (review-gated, generic) --------------------
# R4 evidence_rule — every gate test asserts an explainable constant (analytic value, golden corpus hit, spec-derived invariant — never non-empty/non-black/>0); reviewer verifies 1/255, 1e-6, 152MB cost etc. Mechanical floor is the per-task grep counts (DoD analytic values: T10 uInvViewProj, T8 152MB, T13 BudgetExceeded code, T1 Teapot pixel etc.); the rule itself is review-gated — audit.sh exit 0 + reviewer checklist verifies evidence/regression per gate.
# R3 regression_lock — prior task tests never weakened to make room for new code (review verifies; audit placeholder never matches, reviewer is gate).
# Mechanical weak-assert floor (complements review gate): per-task DoD grep counts are the mechanical floor (T10 uInvViewProj, T8 152 MB, T13 BudgetExceeded code, T1 Teapot pixel 1/255 etc.) — review gate verifies 1/255, 1e-6; bare non-empty/non-black without constant is forbidden by reviewer checklist. No generic regex is used here because `non-empty`/`non-black`/`>0` appear legitimately in docs/TASKS as negative examples (SPEC §4/§6, TASKS R4) and `EXPECT_GT(...,0)` appears in legitimate code (e.g. count checks with analytic 0); the per-task DoD `grep -c "1/255"` / `grep -c "1e-6"` / `grep -c "152 MB"` / `grep -c "640"` / `grep -c "BudgetExceeded"` counts ARE the mechanical floor, reviewer checklist is the second gate. Renamed from `weak_assert_phrase` to `weak_assert_review_gated` to make review-gated nature explicit per spec-review #5.
# Mechanical analytic evidence anchor: at least one GL test asserts an explainable 1/255 or 1e-6 invariant — ensures suite not detached from FR tolerances (per-task DoD grep counts are the floor, this is the audit anchor).
evidence_analytic	require_grep	1/255|1e-6	at least one analytic tolerance constant (1/255 for color, 1e-6 for math) present in sources — evidence rule anchor (per-task DoD grep counts are the floor, this is the audit anchor)
weak_assert_review_gated	forbid_grep	__never_matches_weak_assert_review_gated__	weak assert phrase — mechanical floor is per-task DoD grep counts (analytic 1/255, 1e-6, 152MB); review gate verifies bare non-empty/non-black without constant is forbidden (no generic regex — docs legitimately mention the phrase)
evidence_rule	forbid_grep	__never_matches_evidence_rule__	evidence rule is review-gated: every test asserts an explainable constant (analytic 1/255, 1e-6, 152MB) — reviewer checklist
regression_lock	forbid_grep	__never_matches_regression_lock__	regression lock is review-gated: prior tests never weakened — reviewer checklist

# --- Sanitizer contract (SPEC §5) — catch re-introduction of per-target flags ----------
# V3 T11 defines INTERFACE re_project_sanitizers linked by every re_* target; ad-hoc per-dir -fsanitize blocks deleted.
# This forbid catches direct add_compile_options/add_definitions with -fsanitize outside the INTERFACE target.
no_per_target_sanitize	forbid_grep	add_compile_options.*-fsanitize|add_definitions.*-fsanitize	per-target -fsanitize is forbidden — use INTERFACE re_project_sanitizers linked by every re_* target (T11)

# --- Build hygiene (generic, reinforce here) -----------------------------------
# (built-in checks already cover warning-suppression flags/pragmas)

# --- Comment hygiene: self-contained rationale beside every tag (T15) ----------
# Every comment block that cites a spec/task tag must be understandable WITHOUT
# opening SPEC.md or TASKS.md: it must carry at least 120 characters of
# explanatory prose (counted as non-whitespace chars AFTER removing the tag
# citations themselves, so repeating tags cannot pad the count). The citation
# stays only as trailing provenance. Covered bare-tag shapes:
#   T[0-9]+            task ids (T5, T14)          — word-boundary guarded
#   V[0-9]+\.[0-9a-z]+ iteration/spec aliases (V3.4) — word-boundary guarded
#   SPEC <n>           section citations in both house styles ("SPEC §3" and
#                      the legacy "SPEC S3"; the sweep normalized legacy forms)
# The engine extracts comment blocks (consecutive // lines; a comment after
# code starts its own block; /* */ spans join) from *.h *.hpp *.c *.cpp *.cc
# *.cxx *.glsl under AUDIT_SOURCE_DIRS. Waivers go in
# tools/comment_context.allow, one ERE per line matched against the reported
# `<path>` or `<path>:<line>` — keep it empty; prefer fixing the comment.
comment_tag_context	comment_context	(^|[^[:alnum:]_])(T[0-9]+|V[0-9]+\.[0-9a-z]+)($|[^[:alnum:]_])|SPEC[[:space:]]+(§|S)?[0-9]+	every SPEC/task-tag citation needs >=120 chars of self-contained explanatory prose in its own comment block (state the constraint/design and why; keep the id only as trailing provenance)